## Meta-review

- **A corpus that executes can still fail to discriminate the guard it
  was built to test.** Existence of call+loop is not the same as a
  program the scanner can complete.
- **Source-language tests follow the language, not the MIR feature.**
  `loop/recur` will never grow a same-function back-edge until the
  frontend changes. Hand-written GMIR is the right layer.
- **Do not remove a fallback because the fallback and the guard agree
  on one function.**

## Next

A call+loop the linear scanner can complete (`:cfg-liveness` still
false), or accept all-vreg for all loops. Still missing: call +
back-edge across a spill (`with-scratch-tier-only` / pressure).
kotoba-mir / kotoba-native suites still do not execute compiled
programs.

Do not chase fused-srem, extra MOV, FMA, PGO, kototama optimizer, a
timed `bench` export, or rematching leaf vs LLVM. Do not overwrite
04-21. Do not claim LLVM beaten. Do not remove `back-edge?`."}]
